---
source: crates/aidp-cli/tests/it_compile.rs
expression: redacted
---
version: 5
id: dev-composed
name: ''
description: |
  Demo of pipeline composition — implement a ticket, then reuse the standalone `audit` pipeline as a single `type: pipeline` stage instead of re-declaring its explore/audit/report stages.
kind: pipeline
policy: []
inputs:
  feature:
    required: false
    kind: string
    values: []
    default: null
    description: Optional feature/epic label; feeds run::feature_key, which names the git branch and the vault run folder in place of deriving them from the ticket list.
  jira_keys:
    required: false
    kind: list
    values: []
    default: []
    description: Une ou plusieurs US Jira de la MEME feature, en tableau JSON (ex. ["PIXEL-1","PIXEL-2"])
  prompt:
    required: false
    kind: string
    values: []
    default: ''
    description: ''
  stack:
    required: false
    kind: enum
    values:
    - auto
    - generic
    - rust
    - csharp
    - lambda-ts
    default: auto
    description: Language stack of the repo, which picks the implement stage's language skills via skills_by. auto (default) lets aidp run init detect it from marker files (Cargo.toml, *.sln / *.csproj, serverless.* + package.json); generic keeps the multi-stack skill set.
  target_path:
    required: false
    kind: string
    values: []
    default: src
    description: ''
settings:
  max_correction_iterations: 2
  max_stage_retries: 0
  emit_effort: false
  verify_scope: true
  budget_floor_tokens: 50000
  on_item_failure: pause
  tool_enforcement: off
stages:
- name: prepare_branch
  description: ''
  policy: []
  agent: executor
  skills:
  - git-branch-setup
  needs: []
  inputs:
    branch: feat/{{ feature }}
    jira_keys: '{{ inputs.jira_keys }}'
  outputs:
  - branch.json
  with: {}
  when: 'true'
  body: []
- name: discover_prompt
  description: ''
  policy: []
  agent: analyzer
  skills:
  - graphify-context
  - writing-clearly-and-concisely
  needs:
  - prepare_branch
  inputs:
    request: '{{ inputs.prompt }}'
    task: |
      The demand for this run is the free-text `request` above - there is no Jira ticket. Write prompt_context.md as the requirements note a planner would otherwise get from a ticket, with these sections: (1) Demand - the request restated in one paragraph, plus the verbatim request quoted so nothing is lost in your restatement; (2) Scope - what is in, and an explicit OUT-OF-SCOPE list; a prompt is looser than a ticket, so bounding it is the main value you add here; (3) Acceptance criteria - testable, numbered, derived from the request, each one checkable against code or a test; (4) Assumptions - every gap you filled to make the request actionable, one line each, flagged as an assumption and NOT as a fact; (5) Open questions - what a human must answer, and what you decided to assume in the meantime so the run is not blocked; (6) Affected area - the components and paths the request most likely touches, found via the code graph, so the planner starts from a map rather than from a blank page. Invent no requirement the request does not support. If the request is too vague to bound, say so in one line at the top of the note and still produce the best-effort sections - `plan.md` and the PR gate are where a human stops the run, not this stage.
  outputs:
  - prompt_context.md
  with: {}
  when: '{{ inputs.prompt }}'
  body: []
- name: plan
  description: ''
  policy: []
  agent: planner
  skills:
  - ticket-to-plan-aidp
  needs:
  - prepare_branch
  - discover_prompt
  inputs:
    jira_keys: '{{ inputs.jira_keys }}'
    prompt_context: '{{ stages.discover_prompt.outputs.prompt_context }}'
    task: |
      The demand is in exactly ONE of `jira_keys` (Jira-driven run) or `prompt_context` (prompt-driven run). When `jira_keys` is empty (`[]`) there is no ticket to read and `prompt_context` IS the requirements note: plan from it, and carry its acceptance criteria, assumptions and open questions through into plan.json / plan.md verbatim rather than re-deriving them - on a prompt-driven run they are the only contract the implementation and the audit have. The other mode's stage was skipped at compile time, so neither its file nor the stage directory listed for it under `## Needs (upstream stage_dirs)` exists, which is expected, not an error.
  outputs:
  - plan.json
  - plan.md
  with: {}
  body: []
- name: implement
  description: ''
  policy: []
  agent: executor
  skills: []
  skills_by:
    input: stack
    map:
      csharp:
      - csharp-dev-aidp
      - feature-testing-aidp
      lambda-ts:
      - lambda-ts-dev-aidp
      - feature-testing-aidp
      rust:
      - rust-dev-aidp
      - rust-testing-aidp
    default:
    - csharp-dev-aidp
    - lambda-ts-dev-aidp
    - feature-testing-aidp
  needs:
  - plan
  inputs: {}
  outputs:
  - changed-files.json
  with: {}
  scope:
    mode: repo_wide
    allowed: []
    denied: []
    writes: []
    reads: []
  plan_tasks:
    from: '{{ stages.plan.outputs.plan }}'
    max: 4
    kinds: []
    merge_hint: |
      Apply every shared-file change the tasks deferred to you (wiring, imports, module/DI registration), then build/compile the project and run the FULL test suite once. Fix cross-task breakage and write the consolidated changed-files.json covering every task.
  body: []
- name: qa__explore
  description: ''
  policy: []
  composite_entry: qa
  agent: analyzer
  skills:
  - graphify-context
  needs:
  - implement
  inputs:
    path: '{{ inputs.target_path }}'
  outputs:
  - exploration.md
  with: {}
  body: []
- name: qa__dim_correctness
  description: ''
  policy: []
  agent: reviewer
  skills:
  - graphify-context
  - code-review-aidp
  - code-audit-rubric
  needs:
  - qa__explore
  inputs:
    axis: correctness
    path: '{{ inputs.target_path }}'
  outputs:
  - findings.json
  with: {}
  body: []
- name: qa__dim_security
  description: ''
  policy: []
  agent: reviewer
  skills:
  - graphify-context
  - code-review-aidp
  - code-audit-rubric
  needs:
  - qa__explore
  inputs:
    axis: security
    path: '{{ inputs.target_path }}'
  outputs:
  - findings.json
  with: {}
  body: []
- name: qa__dim_perf
  description: ''
  policy: []
  agent: reviewer
  skills:
  - graphify-context
  - code-review-aidp
  - code-audit-rubric
  needs:
  - qa__explore
  inputs:
    axis: performance
    path: '{{ inputs.target_path }}'
  outputs:
  - findings.json
  with: {}
  body: []
- name: qa__dim_maintainability
  description: ''
  policy: []
  agent: reviewer
  skills:
  - graphify-context
  - code-review-aidp
  - code-audit-rubric
  needs:
  - qa__explore
  inputs:
    axis: maintainability
    path: '{{ inputs.target_path }}'
  outputs:
  - findings.json
  with: {}
  body: []
- name: qa__verify
  description: ''
  policy: []
  agent: reviewer
  model: opus
  skills:
  - graphify-context
  - code-audit-rubric
  needs:
  - qa__dim_correctness
  - qa__dim_security
  - qa__dim_perf
  - qa__dim_maintainability
  inputs: {}
  outputs:
  - confirmed.json
  - scores.json
  with: {}
  body: []
- name: qa__report
  description: ''
  policy: []
  agent: executor
  skills:
  - writing-clearly-and-concisely
  needs:
  - qa__verify
  inputs: {}
  outputs:
  - audit-report.md
  with: {}
  gate: true
  scope:
    mode: stage_dir_only
    allowed: []
    denied: []
    writes: []
    reads: []
  body: []
- name: pr
  description: ''
  policy:
  - Open the PR with `aidp gh pr-create --draft` only when the stage input pr_draft is true; otherwise open a regular PR.
  agent: executor
  skills:
  - git-push
  - writing-clearly-and-concisely
  needs:
  - qa__report
  inputs:
    audit_report: '{{ stages.qa__report.outputs.audit-report }}'
    pr_draft: '{{ settings.pr_draft }}'
  outputs:
  - pr.json
  with: {}
  gate: true
  scope:
    mode: stage_dir_only
    allowed: []
    denied: []
    writes: []
    reads: []
  body: []
